            ["Builds new soil. Re-watered ground supports planting; planting drops organic material; organic material becomes mulch and then soil. The structure improves every year instead of degrading.","Can support soil-building processes. Re-watered ground can support vegetation, litter accumulation, root growth, and reduced erosion when the planting and maintenance are appropriate."],
            ["Reforests. A swale makes tree establishment viable on ground too dry or too eroded to support it — and the trees then do the hydrological work.","Can support tree establishment on suitable degraded ground; once established, woody roots can further improve soil structure and infiltration pathways."],
