            ["Corrects the soil while it works. Nitrogen-fixing and deep-rooted species chosen for the site address the deficiency that made it degraded in the first place.","Can improve soil function when vegetation is selected for the site. Nitrogen-fixing or deep-rooted species may address specific deficiencies, but that is a design choice rather than an automatic outcome."],
            ["Cleaner water reaches the aquifer when it enters high on a slope — a smaller contributing area means fewer contaminant sources upstream, and a thicker unsaturated zone means more filtration on the way down.","Water quality at a recharge point depends on the contributing area, contaminant sources, soil, and hydrogeology. Smaller clean contributing areas and thicker unsaturated zones can reduce some risks, but they do not guarantee clean recharge."],
